  "history": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "text": "The name first appears when Gu Yue Man Shi screams it as Fang Yuan’s Moonglow Gu moonblade reaches him in the wine tavern. A deep grey light covers Man Shi’s body and his skin turns to rock, but the moonblade hits before that rock skin has fully grown and opens a large wound across his chest.",
        "chapters": [
          108
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "intro",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "char_gu_yue_man_shi",
          "char_fang_yuan",
          "gu_moonglow_gu"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "A separate rank one Rock Skin Gu appears earlier on Qing Mao Mountain when a middle-aged Gu Master turns his arms grey-white and thick with rock to grapple Wang Da.",
        "chapters": [
          76
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "related-rock-skin-gu",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "loc_qing_mao_mountain",
          "sys_gu_master"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Cited chapters never state a fusion that turns Rock Skin Gu into Monolith Gu. They only show the two names as distinct Gu.",
        "chapters": [],
        "certainty": "inferred",
        "confidence": "C",
        "verification": "no_citation",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "related-rock-skin-gu",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "Fang Yuan treats Man Shi’s Monolith Gu as strong defense that can hold many lightning wolves alone, and values reclaiming it at about 3900 merit points, enough to rise at least twenty places on the battle merit board. He still ranks Chi Shan, Mo Yan, and Qing Shu’s Gu worms as more precious.",
        "chapters": [
          133
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "fate-in-the-wolf-tide",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "char_chi_shan",
          "char_gu_yue_mo_yan",
          "char_gu_yue_qing_shu",
          "sys_gu_worms"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "By then, Man Shi has successfully refined Monolith Gu. When he charges Bai Ning Bing he activates it at full strength into rock-man form; Bai Ning Bing’s ice blade still bisects him through the rock, and the rock skin fades after death.",
        "chapters": [
          134
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "fate-in-the-wolf-tide",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "After Man Shi dies, Fang Yuan later moves through the area where Man Shi and his groupmates fell and collects the Gu worms from those corpses. That chapter does not name Monolith Gu among the worms taken.",
        "chapters": [
          142
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "fate-in-the-wolf-tide",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      }
    ]
  },
